description: Two gates of the same phase running at once overwrite each other's logs, so a FAIL can point at another run's log.
 
 `gate.sh` keeps each row's output in `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/lw-gate-<phase>/<id>.log`, and its header notes the collision. With several agents sharing the slot pool that happens: two agents gating phase 1 each print the same log path for a FAIL.
 
 Fix: one directory per run (`mktemp -d` under that prefix), printed once when the gate starts, and the FAIL line names the file in it.
